[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-SERVER
TITLE: One stdlib HTTP server serves the app over the resident daemon
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
server.py is one stdlib threaded HTTP server: GET and HEAD only, an allowlisted
static surface, and three JSON routes -- /api/health (the daemon's describe),
/api/graph (the sdoc-board/2 snapshot) and /api/rows (the sdoc-perspective/2
tables). source.py's DaemonSource holds the adapted payloads keyed by daemon
generation and re-exports only when describe reports movement, so a repeat
request costs no export. A NoDaemon refusal becomes HTTP 503 with the remedy in
the body; any other daemon error is a 502.

The ai.strictdoc devenv module builds `sdoc-board` with the same mkScribe
factory and strictdoc virtual-environment runner as the three scribe programs,
then `processes.board` executes that wrapper by absolute Nix store path. The
board therefore shares scribe's interpreter and its pydantic dependency by
construction; no repository launcher or ambient Python lookup sits between
the process manager and server.py.

source.py also builds the snapshot's semantics key, by calling
sdoc_semantics.build_payload over the same parsed grammar the adapter already
reads. The pinned interpreter carries both the semantics engine and the source
extractor used for KIND words. Their lookups remain fail-soft at the adapter
boundary: an import or lookup failure becomes a named refusal or a null label
rather than a missing payload key or a dead process.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 8823edf1 and 46cd3cf1: the static allowlist grew
grammar-groups.json and fsm.js, and source.py gained the semantics payload. The
three JSON routes are unchanged -- semantics rides inside /api/graph rather
than on a fourth route.

Updated 2026-09-08 for commit 8b936c3c: the allowlist grew two more entries,
/assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-api.js and /assets/vendor/elkjs/elk-worker.min.js, and
they are the only ones not backed by a file in this directory -- server.py
resolves them against the Nix store path in SDOC_BOARD_ELKJS_DIR and refuses to
start when that variable is unset or does not hold both files. Still three JSON
routes.

Updated 2026-09-09 by WORK-BOARD-SERVE-PINS-ITS-INTERPRETER: the ambient
docs/sdoc/board/serve launcher was deleted. The strictdoc devenv module now
packages server.py as `sdoc-board`, launches its absolute store path as the
board process, and shares the strictdoc virtual-environment interpreter used by
scribe. The interpreter-launchers check guards the boundary with the removed
launcher as its positive control.
<<<
